# Push a change to this file to run a backtest without the GitHub connector.
# Format: one line, "MODE [MONTHS]". Lines starting with # are ignored.
# The mode must also be in the fetch-step whitelist in backtest.yml, or it will
# silently get the short-history fetcher (see the v78bt note in CLAUDE.md).
#
# v84bt: Wyckoff. The method splits into pieces that are already deployed (the
# breakout out of a range IS Donchian), already rejected (volume as a filter,
# spring-as-a-reversal, stops beyond the shakeout, smart-money tilt) or not
# codeable at all (phase labelling). Two constructs survive the triage and are
# genuinely untested here: SPRING (did a shakeout precede this breakout) and
# EFFORT/RESULT (did the breakout bar buy its movement cheaply). Part A asks
# whether they separate the trades at all before any tilt is built on them.
v84bt 36
